{{also|émission|Emission}}
==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=emission}}

===Etymology===
First attested in 1607. {{borrowing|la|emissio|ēmissiō|sending forth}} (also possibly influenced by {{etyl|frm}} {{term|emission|lang=frm}} from the same Latin source) from {{term|emitto|ēmittō|send out|lang=la}}, from {{term|ex||from, out of|lang=la}} + {{term|mitto|mittō|send|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɪʃən}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# That which is emitted or sent out.
#: {{usex|the '''emission''' was mostly blood}}
# The act of sending or throwing out; the act of sending forth or putting into circulation; issue.
#: {{usex|the '''emission''' of light from the sun}}
#: {{usex|the '''emission''' of heat from a fire}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|outsending}}

